const stories = [
 {id:'gate',title:'Before the room believed him',subtitle:'Ashtavakra at Janaka’s court',culture:'Indian epic',time:'3 min',theme:'When you feel underestimated',sourceTitle:'Mahabharata, Vana Parva, sections CXXXII–CXXXIV',source:'https://sacred-texts.com/hin/m03/m03133.htm',sourceId:'mahabharata',sensitive:false,question:'Where am I treating someone else’s first impression as the whole truth about me?',questionHi:'Kya main kisi aur ki pehli rai ko apni poori pehchaan maan raha hoon?',anchor:'Someone’s first impression is not the whole of me.',blocks:[['At the threshold','In the Mahabharata, the young Ashtavakra arrives at King Janaka’s sacrifice with his uncle, Swetaketu. A gatekeeper tells him that boys are not admitted: this assembly is for learned elders. Before his ideas can be heard, his age has already been judged.','Kabhi-kabhi humari baat sunne se pehle hi humare baare mein faisla ho jaata hai.'],['More than a first impression','Ashtavakra argues that age and appearance do not settle a person’s knowledge. He gains entry, exchanges questions with Janaka, and goes on to challenge Vandin. The epic’s surrounding account includes a curse, disability, a threatening contest, and a supernatural resolution. It is a complex ancient story, not a modern lesson in fairness.','Kisi ki nazar mein chhota hona, aapki poori pehchaan nahi hai.'],['A gentler reading for today','One way to reflect on the gate is to notice the voices we carry inside: “You are too young,” “You do not look right,” or “You do not belong.” You can question a judgment without having to prove yourself through a contest. Your worth does not depend on winning, being exceptional, or changing your body.','Apni kadar ke liye har baar jeetna ya khud ko prove karna zaroori nahi.']]},
 {id:'waves',title:'You, and the passing wave',subtitle:'A reflection with the Ashtavakra Gita',culture:'Indian philosophy',time:'3 min',theme:'When your thoughts feel like all of you',sourceTitle:'Ashtavakra Gita, chapter II, verses 23–25',source:'https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Ashtavakra_Gita#Chapter_II',sourceId:'ashtavakra-gita',sensitive:false,question:'Could I describe this as “I’m noticing a worried thought” rather than a final verdict about myself?',questionHi:'Kya main keh sakta hoon “ek pareshan karne wala khayal aa raha hai,” bina use apni poori sachchai maane?',anchor:'This feeling deserves care. It does not have to define all of me.',blocks:[['A different kind of text','The Ashtavakra Gita is a philosophical dialogue between Ashtavakra and Janaka. It is distinct from the Mahabharata’s court episode. Its nondual teaching uses images of an ocean and waves to explore awareness and identity. You do not need to adopt its spiritual beliefs to consider an image.','Yeh ek darshanik baatcheet hai. Isse kuch samajhne ke liye aapko apne vishwas badalne ki zaroorat nahi.'],['The wave and the ocean','In chapter II, waves arise in an ocean as the wind moves. For a present-day reflection, a thought might be imagined as a wave: noticeable, sometimes powerful, and changing. The metaphor does not mean your difficulty is unreal. It also does not promise that distress will disappear if you simply observe it.','Feeling sach mein mushkil ho sakti hai. Use notice karna, use jhootha kehna nahi hai.'],['A little space around the thought','If it feels comfortable, try naming what is here: “I notice worry,” or “I feel hurt right now.” Then ask what care this moment needs: a pause, a practical step, or another person. If observing your inner experience feels uncomfortable or makes you feel detached, leave the metaphor and look around the room instead.','Abhi mujhe kis cheez ki zaroorat hai: thoda rukna, ek chhota kadam, ya kisi ka saath?']]},
 {id:'oedipus',title:'When a question takes over',subtitle:'Reading Oedipus with care',culture:'Greek tragedy',time:'4 min',theme:'A reflection on uncertainty and responsibility',sourceTitle:'Sophocles, Oedipus the King, opening investigation and Tiresias scene; Jebb translation',source:'https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Tragedies_of_Sophocles_(Jebb_1917)/Oedipus_the_King',sourceId:'oedipus',sensitive:true,question:'What genuinely needs an answer today, and what can wait until I have more support?',questionHi:'Aaj kis sawal ka jawab zaroori hai, aur kis sawal ke liye main waqt aur sahara le sakta hoon?',anchor:'I can seek understanding at a pace I can support.',blocks:[['An investigation begins','In Sophocles’ tragedy, Thebes is suffering, and Oedipus takes responsibility for finding the cause. He seeks information about the killing of the former king, Laius. In the encounter with Tiresias, uncertainty, accusation, and anger begin to narrow the conversation.','Jab jawab nahi milta, toh kabhi-kabhi baat samajhne ki jagah hum aarop aur darr mein phans jaate hain.'],['The story is not your destiny','The play later reveals tragic family connections and includes suicide and self-injury. It is not evidence that seeking truth is dangerous, that anxiety predicts tragedy, or that family harm is someone’s fate. The literary character and the later psychoanalytic idea called the “Oedipus complex” are different things; this app uses neither to diagnose you.','Yeh kahaani aapka bhavishya ya aapki diagnosis nahi hai.'],['A present-day question','A possible reflection is about how we meet uncertainty. Are we gathering useful information, or repeatedly asking a question without anything new to work with? This is a prompt to explore, not a claim about what caused your thoughts. When a question feels too large, it may help to identify one practical piece and seek a trusted person’s perspective.','Har sawal abhi solve karna zaroori nahi. Kisi ka saath lekar ek hissa samajhna bhi ek kadam hai.']]}
];
let bilingual=true,selected=[],nuance='',context='',intensity=3,route='',draft='',thoughts=[],sorts={},resetStep=0,resetDone=false,readerScale=17,libraryQuery='',allowIntense=false,sourceManifest=null;
let nextStep='';
let anchors=[];try{const saved=JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem('antar-anchors')||'[]');if(Array.isArray(saved))anchors=saved.filter(x=>typeof x==='string').slice(0,100);}catch{}
const sourceCache=new Map();
const hi=t=>bilingual?`<span class="hinglish">${esc(t)}</span>`:'';
const currentMood=()=>moodData.find(m=>m.id===selected[0])||moodData.find(m=>m.id==='unsure');
const button=(text,action,cls='primary')=>`<button class="${cls}" data-action="${action}">${text}</button>`;
function toast(text){$('#toast').textContent=text;$('#toast').classList.add('show');clearTimeout(toast.timer);toast.timer=setTimeout(()=>$('#toast').classList.remove('show'),2600)}
function art(kind='sanctuary'){
 const sky=kind==='oedipus'?'#e9e5ef':kind==='gate'?'#e8d9bc':'#dce9e3';
 return `<svg viewBox="0 0 380 150" preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid slice" aria-hidden="true"><rect width="380" height="150" fill="${sky}"/><circle cx="${kind==='gate'?270:280}" cy="40" r="24" fill="#f0c58f"/><path d="M0 128Q100 70 190 112T380 100V150H0" fill="#b4cbc0"/><path d="M0 145Q100 114 200 133T380 123V150H0" fill="#779e91"/>${kind==='oedipus'?'<path d="M90 48H190V57H90zM95 57H108V125H95zM129 57H142V125H129zM163 57H176V125H163zM83 125H197V133H83z" fill="#777b95"/>':kind==='gate'?'<path d="M75 140V61a48 48 0 0 1 96 0v79H153V62a30 30 0 0 0-60 0v78Z" fill="#8b9984"/><circle cx="123" cy="108" r="6" fill="#3e625b"/><path d="M114 133L117 116H129L133 133Z" fill="#3e625b"/>':'<path d="M96 150V67a44 44 0 0 1 88 0v83M111 150V69a29 29 0 0 1 58 0v81" fill="none" stroke="#fbfcf5" stroke-width="2"/><path d="M232 143Q258 124 281 138M218 149Q246 134 267 149" fill="none" stroke="#ecf3ed" stroke-width="2"/>'}</svg>`
}
function storyCard(s,reason=''){return `<a class="story-card" href="#story/${s.id}"><div class="story-art">${art(s.id)}</div><div class="story-copy"><div class="meta">${esc(s.culture)} · ${s.time}${s.sensitive?' · Sensitive themes':''}</div><h3>${esc(s.title)}</h3><p>${esc(reason||s.theme)}</p><span class="read-label">Read the reflection ↗</span></div></a>`}
function home(){const hr=new Date().getHours();return `<section class="hero"><a class="install-link" href="#install">Antar on your home screen</a><p class="greeting">${hr<12?'A softer start':hr<18?'A pause in your day':'A little space this evening'}</p><h1>Aaj mann mein<br>kya chal raha hai?</h1><p class="sub">Do-teen chhote choices. Phir ek reflection, aur chaaho toh kahaani.${hi('Jaisa bhi lag raha hai, yahan se shuru kar sakte hain.')}</p><div class="hero-art">${art()}</div></section><button class="choice" data-go="mood"><span class="symbol">◌</span><span><strong>Feeling ko samjhein</strong><small>Words chuno. Dheere se samjhein.</small></span><span class="chevron">›</span></button><button class="choice soft" data-action="start-reset"><span class="symbol">≈</span><span><strong>Less thinking. Just a pause.</strong><small>No typing. Go at your own pace.</small></span><span class="chevron">›</span></button><div class="home-shortcuts"><a href="#month"><span>▦</span><strong>Mera mahina</strong><small>${checkins.length?checkins.length+' saved moments':'Patterns, at your pace'}</small></a><a href="#play"><span>◇</span><strong>Thodi kahaani</strong><small>Choices. No scores.</small></a></div><div class="personal-shortcuts"><a class="choice soft" href="#mind"><span class="symbol">≋</span><span><strong>My second mind</strong><small>Sab yahin rakh do. Sort later, or never.</small></span></a><a class="install-link" href="#comfort">My comfort shelf</a></div><div class="section-head"><h2>What’s here today?</h2><a href="#mood" class="text-btn">Explore feelings</a></div><div class="mood-row">${moodData.slice(0,6).map(m=>`<button class="mood-chip" data-quick="${m.id}">${m.name}${bilingual?`<span>${m.id==='overwhelmed'?'Sab kuch ek saath':m.id==='anxious'?'Ghabrahat':m.id==='looping'?'Khayalon ka chakkar':m.id==='sad'?'Udaasi':m.id==='lonely'?'Akelaapan':'Khud ko kam samajhna'}</span>`:''}</button>`).join('')}</div><div class="section-head"><h2>A story to sit with</h2><a href="#library" class="text-btn">The library</a></div>${storyCard(stories[1])}<p class="note"><a href="#toolkit">Open my anchors</a><br>Nothing to catch up on. No streak to keep.<br>Just a space to return to when you need it.</p>`}
function mood(){return `${button('‹ Sanctuary','go-home','back')}<h1>Let’s find your words.</h1><p class="sub">Choose up to three. Mixed feelings belong here, too.${hi('Ek feeling ya kai saath mein. Jo fit ho, wahi chunna.')}</p><div class="mood-grid">${moodData.map(m=>`<button class="mood-tile ${selected.includes(m.id)?'selected':''}" data-mood="${m.id}" aria-pressed="${selected.includes(m.id)}"><span class="glyph">${m.glyph}</span><strong>${m.name}</strong>${hi(m.hi)}</button>`).join('')}</div>${button(`Explore this feeling${selected.length>1?' mix':''}`,'refine')}${button('Abhi naam nahi dena','unnamed-feeling','text-btn')}${button('I’d rather take a quiet pause','start-reset','secondary')}<p class="note">These are everyday descriptions, not diagnoses. You get the final say on what fits.</p>`}
function refine(){return quickRefine()}
function recommendedStory(){const m=currentMood();const s=stories.find(x=>x.id===m.story);return intensity>=4||s.sensitive&&!allowIntense?stories[1]:s}
const supportTips={"overwhelmed": ["Make one thing smaller", "What is one demand you could postpone, reduce, or ask for help with today?", "Aaj kis ek cheez ka bojh thoda kam kar sakte ho?"], "anxious": ["Separate a fact from a possibility", "What do you know right now? What is still a prediction? You do not need to settle every possibility.", "Abhi kya pata hai, aur kya sirf andesha hai?"], "looping": ["Check what another round would add", "Has any new information arrived? If not, you can leave the question open for a while and choose a different activity.", "Kya nayi jaankari mili hai, ya wahi sawal phir aa raha hai?"], "sad": ["Let the next step be gentle", "Would comfort, company, or less pressure fit better right now? Pick just one.", "Abhi tasalli, saath, ya thoda kam pressure chahiye?"], "lonely": ["Look for a small connection", "Is there someone you could send a simple hello to, or spend a little time alongside?", "Kya kisi ko ek chhota sa hello bhej sakte ho?"], "ashamed": ["Try a kinder description", "Describe what happened without turning it into a verdict about your whole self. What would you say to a friend?", "Jo hua use batao, apne poore aap ko galat mat thehrao."], "guilty": ["Find what is actually yours", "Is there a specific repair you want to make, or are you taking responsibility for something outside your control?", "Kya kuch sudharna hai, ya aap apne hisse se zyada zimmedari le rahe ho?"], "angry": ["Give your next response some space", "If it is safe, pause before replying. What boundary or need would you like to express when you are ready?", "Reply se pehle thodi jagah. Kaunsi zaroorat ya had batani hai?"], "numb": ["Start outside the feeling", "You do not need to force an emotion. Try noticing an ordinary object, or a comfortable texture nearby.", "Feeling ko force nahi karna. Aas-paas ki koi cheez notice kar sakte ho."], "exhausted": ["Lower the size of the task", "Could you choose rest, a basic need, or a two-minute version of what you intended?", "Kaam ka chhota version, koi basic zaroorat, ya aaram?"], "uncertain": ["Choose a reversible step", "What is one small thing you could try without having to decide your whole future?", "Poora future tay kiye bina, kya chhota sa try kar sakte ho?"], "jealous": ["Listen for what matters underneath", "Does this comparison point to something you value or want? You can name that need without judging yourself for it.", "Comparison ke neeche kaunsi khwahish ya zaroorat hai?"], "restless": ["Offer the energy a gentle outlet", "If comfortable and safe, change your position or take a short walk. Or use the quiet reset while staying seated.", "Comfortable ho toh position badlo, ya baith kar reset karo."], "hurt": ["Name the need before the reply", "Was it respect, care, honesty, or belonging that felt missing? There is no need to solve the relationship this minute.", "Kis cheez ki kami lagi: izzat, care, sachchai, ya apnapan?"], "okay": ["Notice what is already enough", "Is there something about this moment you would like to remember? You do not have to turn it into a goal.", "Is pal ki koi chhoti si baat yaad rakhna chahoge?"], "unsure": ["A label is optional", "You can begin with what you need: less noise, some company, a pause, or space to put your thoughts.", "Naam na mile toh bhi, apni zaroorat se shuru kar sakte ho."]};
function personalTip(){const t=supportTips[currentMood().id];return `<div class="panel"><h3>${esc(t[0])}</h3><p>${esc(t[1])}${hi(t[2])}</p>${selected.length>1?'<p class="small">This prompt follows your first selected feeling. You can explore a different feeling or choose another path.</p>':''}</div>`}
function support(){const m=currentMood(),s=recommendedStory();return `${button('‹ Refine the feeling','go-refine','back')}<p class="greeting">A starting point, chosen by you</p><h1>${intensity>=4?'Let’s make this moment smaller.':'A little room around '+(selected.length>1?'these feelings.':'this feeling.')}</h1><div class="panel"><strong>${selected.map(id=>esc(moodData.find(m=>m.id===id).name)).join(' + ')}</strong>${hi(m.hi)}${nuance?`<p>${esc(nuance)}</p>`:''}${context?`<p>In your words: ${esc(context)}</p>`:''}<p class="small">Intensity: ${intensity}/5. These labels are yours to change.</p></div>${understandingReflection()}${pastHelpPanel(true)}<button class="choice" data-action="start-reset"><span class="symbol">≈</span><span><strong>${intensity>=4?'Start with the room around you':'A quiet reset'}</strong><small>Notice your surroundings, one prompt at a time</small></span><span class="chevron">›</span></button><button class="choice soft" data-go="untangle"><span class="symbol">≋</span><span><strong>Put the thoughts somewhere</strong><small>Choose what needs attention and what can wait</small></span><span class="chevron">›</span></button>${['lonely','hurt','sad'].some(id=>selected.includes(id))?`<div class="panel"><h3>A person can be an anchor.</h3><p>You could tell someone you trust: “I’m having a difficult moment. Could you sit with me or check in?”</p>${button('Keep that message in my anchors','save-connection','secondary')}</div>`:''}${passageRecommendations()}<details><summary>A longer original reflection</summary>${storyCard(s,s.id==='gate'?'A reflection on being judged and knowing your own worth.':'A philosophical image for exploring the space around a feeling.')}</details>${button('Is moment ko log karna hai','new-checkin','secondary')}${button('Thodi interactive kahaani?','go-play','secondary')}${button('I need more support','go-help','text-btn')}`}
const resetPrompts=[['5','Notice five things you can see.','Shapes, light, a familiar object. No need to name them here.','Paanch cheezein dekho. Bas apne aas-paas.'],['4','Notice four things you can feel.','The chair beneath you, fabric, or another comfortable texture.','Chaar cheezon ka sparsh notice karo. Jo comfortable ho.'],['3','Notice three things you can hear.','Nearby or far away. A quiet sound counts.','Teen awaazein suno. Dheemi awaaz bhi kaafi hai.'],['2','Notice two things you can smell.','If nothing comes to mind, you can skip this.','Do khushboo notice karo. Na ho toh skip kar sakte ho.'],['1','Notice one thing you can taste.','Or simply pause here. There is no right answer.','Ek swaad notice karo. Ya bas yahin thoda ruk jao.']];
function reset(){if(resetDone)return `<div class="quiet"><div class="quiet-orb">◌</div><h1>You can stop here.</h1><p>A little pause is enough. You do not need to feel different for this to count.${hi('Behtar mehsoos karna koi test nahi hai.')}</p></div><button class="primary" data-gentle="reset-followup">Ab kaisa lag raha hai? Optional check-in</button>${button('This helped · keep it in my anchors','save-reset','secondary')}${button('Try something else','go-support','secondary')}${button('Back to sanctuary','go-home','text-btn')}`;const p=resetPrompts[resetStep];return `${button('‹ Leave the reset','go-home','back')}<div class="progress" aria-label="Step ${resetStep+1} of 5">${resetPrompts.map((_,i)=>`<span class="${i<=resetStep?'done':''}"></span>`).join('')}</div><div class="quiet"><div class="quiet-orb" aria-hidden="true">${p[0]}</div><h2>${p[1]}</h2><p>${p[2]}${hi(p[3])}</p></div>${button(resetStep===4?'Finish the pause':'I’m ready for the next prompt','reset-next')}${button('Skip this sense','reset-next','text-btn')}<p class="note">Keep your eyes open if that feels better. Skip any sense or stop at any time. <a href="https://www.nhsinform.scot/healthy-living/mental-wellbeing/breathing-and-relaxation-exercises/grounding-exercises" target="_blank" rel="noopener">About this grounding exercise</a></p>`}
function untangle(){return `${button('‹ My next step','go-support','back')}<h1>A place for the noise.</h1><p class="sub">One thought per line, or just write freely.${hi('Perfect likhna zaroori nahi. Jo mann mein hai, likh do.')}</p><label class="field" for="thought-draft">What’s taking up space?</label><textarea id="thought-draft" maxlength="12000" placeholder="I keep thinking about…">${esc(draft)}</textarea><p class="small">Not sent anywhere or saved to your anchors. Cleared when this page reloads or you choose “Clear this session.”</p>${button('Help me sort this','sort-thoughts')}${button('Clear this session','clear-session','text-btn')}<p class="note">You’ll choose what needs attention. Your thoughts won’t be automatically interpreted.</p>`}
function sorting(){return `${button('‹ Back to my words','go-untangle','back')}<h1>One thought at a time.</h1><p class="sub">You decide where each one belongs. Leaving a thought unsorted is okay.</p>${thoughts.map((t,i)=>`<div class="thought"><p>${esc(t)}</p><div class="chips">${['One small action','Can wait','Need support'].map(label=>`<button class="chip ${sorts[i]===label?'selected':''}" data-sort="${i}" data-bucket="${label}" aria-pressed="${sorts[i]===label}">${label}</button>`).join('')}</div></div>`).join('')}<div class="panel"><h3>What would make the next ten minutes easier?</h3><p>Choose a step small enough for the energy you have. Reaching out or resting can be a step, too.</p><label class="field" for="next-step">An optional next step</label><input id="next-step" type="text" maxlength="200" value="${esc(nextStep)}" placeholder="For example: ask for more time"><div id="step-status" class="status" role="status"></div>${button('Keep only this step in my anchors','save-step','secondary')}</div>${button('Done · let the draft go','finish-thoughts')}<p class="note">“Can wait” has no reminder attached. You are free to come back when you choose.</p>`}
function bookMatches(s,q){return [s.title,s.author,s.translator,...(s.tags||[])].join(' ').toLowerCase().includes(q.toLowerCase())}
function library(){const q=libraryQuery.toLowerCase(),filtered=stories.filter(s=>(allowIntense||!s.sensitive)&&[s.title,s.subtitle,s.culture,s.theme].join(' ').toLowerCase().includes(q));return `<h1>A library for<br>looking inward.</h1><p class="sub">Stories and philosophy. Your own meaning.${hi('Alag-alag nazariye. Apna matlab khud khojo.')}</p><a class="passage-entry" href="#passages"><strong>Explore passages by feeling</strong><span>${excerptBank?excerptBank.length+' verified excerpts':'Source-linked excerpts'} · Hinglish interpretations · Your choice of reading need</span></a><label class="field" for="library-search">Find a story, book or author</label><input id="library-search" type="search" value="${esc(libraryQuery)}" placeholder="Try Kafka, Machiavelli, anger, identity…"><section id="reflections" ${q&&!filtered.length?'hidden':''}><div class="section-head"><h2>Short reflections</h2></div><label class="field"><input id="intense" type="checkbox" ${allowIntense?'checked':''}>Include intense story reflections</label><p class="small">Oedipus includes family violence, incest, suicide, and self-injury. This switch controls short reflections; full books have separate content notes.</p><div id="story-results">${filtered.length?filtered.map(s=>storyCard(s)).join(''):'<p class="empty">No short reflection matches. Try the book shelf below.</p>'}</div></section><div class="section-head"><h2>The book shelf</h2><span class="small">${sourceManifest?.sources?.length||'…'} sources</span></div><p class="small">Complete downloaded editions and extracted readings. Open a book for its content note, chapters, and download. Original editions are in English; Hinglish is used in mood descriptions and app reflections.</p><div id="book-results" class="sources-list">${sourcesHTML(libraryQuery)}</div>`}
function sourcesHTML(query=''){if(!sourceManifest)return '<p class="small">Loading the book shelf…</p>';const items=sourceManifest.sources||[];const entries=items.map((s,i)=>({s,i})).filter(({s})=>bookMatches(s,query));return entries.length?entries.map(({s,i})=>`<a class="book-card" href="#source/${i}"><span class="book-spine" aria-hidden="true">▤</span><span><span class="small">${esc(s.author||'')}</span><h3>${esc(s.title)}</h3><span class="small">${s.epub?'EPUB + chapter reader':'PDF + extracted reader'}</span>${s.tags?.length?`<span class="book-tags">${s.tags.map(esc).join(' · ')}</span>`:''}</span><span aria-hidden="true">›</span></a>`).join(''):'<p class="empty">No books match. Try an author’s name or a different topic.</p>'}

function storyView(id){const s=stories.find(s=>s.id===id);if(!s)return notFound();return `${button('‹ Story library','go-library','back')}<div class="story-art" style="border-radius:23px">${art(s.id)}</div><div class="reading-top"><span class="tag">${s.culture} · ${s.time}</span><h1>${s.title}</h1><p class="sub">${s.subtitle}</p></div>${s.sensitive?`<div class="warning"><strong>Before you read</strong><p>This reflection refers to a story involving family violence, incest, suicide, and self-injury. No graphic descriptions are included. The original text is more explicit.</p><a href="#story/waves">Choose a gentler reading</a></div>`:''}<p class="small">An original reflection inspired by the source. Not a translation, diagnosis, or treatment.</p><div class="read-controls"><span class="small">Reading size</span><div><button data-size="-1" aria-label="Smaller reading text">A−</button> <button data-size="1" aria-label="Larger reading text">A+</button></div></div><article class="reader" style="font-size:${readerScale}px">${s.blocks.map(([h,p,hp])=>`<h2>${h}</h2><p>${p}${hi(hp)}</p>`).join('')}</article><div class="panel"><h3>A question, if you want one</h3><p>${s.question}${hi(s.questionHi)}</p><p class="small">No answer to submit. A different interpretation is welcome.</p></div>${button('Keep a line in my anchors',`save-story:${s.id}`,'secondary')}<p class="small">The line: “${s.anchor}”</p><div class="source"><strong>Where this comes from</strong><p>${esc(s.sourceTitle)}.</p><a href="${s.source}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read the source online ↗</a><br><a href="#source/${s.id==='gate'?'2/1':s.id==='waves'?'1/1':'0/0'}">Read the matching extracted chapter or section</a><br><a href="#sources">Open the downloaded source library</a><p>Hinglish descriptions are informal paraphrases written for this app. Myth-to-mood connections are editorial suggestions, not established clinical findings.</p></div>${button('Come back to this moment','start-reset','secondary')}`}
function toolkit(){return `<h1>Your anchors.</h1><a class="install-link" href="#comfort">My comfort shelf · photos, audio, people &amp; words</a><br><a class="install-link" href="#mind">My second mind · a place for thoughts</a><p class="sub">A few things you chose to keep. No daily tasks.${hi('Jo aapke kaam aaye, bas wahi yahan rakho.')}</p>${anchors.length?anchors.map((a,i)=>`<div class="anchor"><p>${esc(a)}</p><button data-remove="${i}" aria-label="Remove anchor ${i+1}">Remove</button></div>`).join(''):'<div class="panel"><h3>There’s room for what helps.</h3><p>Save a helpful line from a story, a quiet reset, or add something that already works for you.</p></div>'}<label class="field" for="anchor-input">Something worth remembering</label><input id="anchor-input" type="text" maxlength="400" placeholder="A walk on the terrace. A friend. A song.">${button('Add my anchor','add-anchor')}<p class="note">Only anchors you choose to save are stored in this browser on this device. They are not encrypted by the app or synced. Clearing website data removes them.</p>${anchors.length?button('Delete all saved anchors','delete-anchors','text-btn'):''}`}
function settings(){return `<h1>A space with boundaries.</h1><div class="panel"><h3>Your words stay with you.</h3><p>Unsaved thought drafts and mood choices stay in this open page’s memory. A check-in is saved only when you choose Save. Saved check-ins and anchors are not sent to AI or synced to an account.</p><p>Anchors and check-ins you explicitly save go into this browser’s local storage. Check-ins can contain feelings, needs, times, situations, notes, and optional helpfulness feedback. Needs-map confirmations and corrections are also kept locally. Second mind thoughts and comfort media you explicitly save use this browser’s local database, without app encryption or account sync. Anyone with access to this browser profile may see them.</p></div><a class="text-btn" href="#month">My month, exports, and saved check-in controls</a><h2>What Antar can offer</h2><p class="sub">A place to understand feeling words, log difficult moments, notice descriptive patterns, explore interactive stories, and reflect through literature. It cannot diagnose conditions, provide therapy, monitor safety, or promise recovery.</p><div class="divider"></div><h2>About the reading library</h2><p class="sub">We separate ancient sources, named translations, and our own interpretations. Disability, pain, and family conflict are not signs of spiritual failure. You can leave any story or exercise.</p><a class="text-btn" href="#sources">View editions, rights and original texts</a><div class="divider"></div><h2>Antar on your phone</h2><a class="install-link" href="#install">Install &amp; offline mode</a><p class="sub">In Safari, open Share, then “Add to Home Screen.” The website can open in its own app-style window. Install Antar and optionally prepare its offline space.</p><div class="divider"></div><h2>Privacy in practice</h2><p class="sub">There is no third-party analytics service or advertising in the app. Check-in observations and saved-feedback learning are computed in this browser. Hosting and sign-in providers may process standard access information. Fonts are hosted with the app; source links open external sites. This is a personal prototype, not a secure clinical record system.</p><a class="install-link" href="#install">Install &amp; offline mode</a>${button('Clear current session','clear-session','secondary')}${button('Delete all saved anchors','delete-anchors','secondary')}${button('Find human support','go-help','text-btn')}`}
function help(){return `${button('‹ Sanctuary','go-home','back')}<h1>You deserve support beyond a screen.</h1><p class="sub">If feelings keep disrupting sleep, work, relationships, or daily life, a qualified mental health professional can help you work through them.</p><div class="panel"><h3>Make reaching out smaller.</h3><p>“I’ve been overwhelmed and could use some support. Could we talk, or could you help me find a professional?”</p>${button('Keep this message','save-connection','secondary')}</div><p class="sub">If you feel in immediate danger or might act on thoughts of harming yourself, contact your local emergency service or go to the nearest emergency department. If possible, stay with someone you trust.</p><p class="note">Antar is not monitored and cannot contact help for you.</p>`}
function notFound(){return `<h1>This page isn’t here.</h1><p class="sub">Let’s return to a familiar place.</p>${button('Back to sanctuary','go-home')}`}
function sourcePage(index){const item=sourceManifest?.sources?.[index];if(!item)return notFound();return `${button('‹ Book shelf','go-library','back')}<p class="greeting">${esc(item.author||'')}</p><h1>${esc(item.title)}</h1><p class="sub">${esc(item.translator||'')} ${item.translator?'translation':''}</p><div class="warning"><strong>Before you read</strong><p>${esc(item.contentNote||'Historical literature can contain violence and dated views. Read only if this feels right today.')}</p></div><p class="small">${esc(item.edition||'')}</p>${item.epub?`<a class="download-book" href="${esc(item.epub)}" download>Download EPUB for Apple Books</a>`:''}${item.pdf?`<a class="download-book" href="${esc(item.pdf)}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open original PDF</a>`:''}${item.licenseNotice?`<div class="license-notice"><p>${esc(item.licenseNotice)}</p><a href="${esc(item.licenseUrl)}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read the full Project Gutenberg License</a></div>`:''}${relatedPassages(item.id)}<label class="field" for="section-select">Choose a chapter or section</label><select id="section-select" class="section-select"><option>Loading chapters…</option></select><div class="read-controls"><span class="small">Reading size</span><div><button data-size="-1" aria-label="Smaller reading text">A−</button> <button data-size="1" aria-label="Larger reading text">A+</button></div></div><p id="source-locator" class="source"></p><article id="source-text" class="fulltext reader" style="font-size:${readerScale}px"><p class="sub">Loading extracted source text…</p></article><p class="note">Extracted text may contain OCR or line-break errors. Check the original edition when wording matters.</p><details><summary>Edition, attribution and reuse</summary><p class="small">${esc(item.rights||'')}</p><p class="small">${esc(item.rightsEvidence||'')}</p><div class="sources-list">${item.original?`<a href="${esc(item.original)}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open original source with notices</a>`:''}<a href="${esc(item.sourceUrl)}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Publisher / source record</a></div></details>`}

function go(path){if(location.hash==='#'+path)render();else location.hash=path}
function render(keepScroll=false){route=location.hash.slice(1)||'home';const prior=scrollY;const renderers={mind:secondMind,comfort:comfortShelf,after:gentleFollowup,'after-saved':gentleReceipt,install:installView,home,mood,refine,support:supportForNow,reset,untangle,sort:sorting,library,toolkit,settings,help,history:fullHistory,needs:needsMap,memory:memoryView,month:monthView,log:checkinForm,play:storyPlayroom,passages:passageCatalog,sources:()=>`${button('‹ Story library','go-library','back')}<h1>The source shelf.</h1><p class="sub">Literature, mythology, and philosophy. Downloaded editions with chapter readers and source details.</p><div class="sources-list">${sourcesHTML()}</div>`};$('#main').innerHTML=route.startsWith('play/')?playFable(route.split('/')[1]):route.startsWith('excerpt/')?excerptView(route.split('/')[1]):route.startsWith('story/')?storyView(route.split('/')[1]):route.startsWith('source/')?sourcePage(Number(route.split('/')[1])):(renderers[route]||notFound)();document.querySelectorAll('[data-nav]').forEach(n=>{const active=n.dataset.nav===route||(n.dataset.nav==='month'&&['log','history','needs','memory'].includes(route))||(n.dataset.nav==='play'&&route.startsWith('play/'))||(n.dataset.nav==='mood'&&['refine','support','untangle','sort','reset','after','after-saved'].includes(route))||(n.dataset.nav==='library'&&/^(story|source|excerpt|passages)/.test(route));n.classList.toggle('active',active);if(active)n.setAttribute('aria-current','page');else n.removeAttribute('aria-current')});$('#language').textContent=bilingual?'Meanings on':'Meanings off';if(!keepScroll){window.scrollTo(0,0);$('#main').focus({preventScroll:true})}else window.scrollTo(0,prior);if(route.startsWith('source/'))loadSection(Number(route.split('/')[1]),Number(route.split('/')[2])||0);}
async function loadSection(index,sectionIndex){
 const key=route;const items=sourceManifest?.sources||[],item=items[index];if(!item)return;
 const target=$('#source-text');if(!target)return;
 try{let sections=sourceCache.get(item.id);if(!sections){const r=await fetch(item.text);if(!r.ok)throw Error();sections=await r.json();if(!Array.isArray(sections)||!sections.length)throw Error();sourceCache.set(item.id,sections);}
 if(route!==key||!target.isConnected)return;
 const section=sections[sectionIndex]||sections[0];const selector=$('#section-select');selector.innerHTML=sections.map((s,i)=>`<option value="${i}">${esc(s.title)}</option>`).join('');selector.value=String(sections.indexOf(section));
 target.textContent=section.text;
 const excerptId=route.split('/')[3];const focused=excerptBank?.find(e=>e.id===excerptId&&e.sourceId===item.id&&e.sectionIndex===sections.indexOf(section));
 if(focused){target.innerHTML=esc(section.text.slice(0,focused.start))+'<mark id="passage-focus" tabindex="-1">'+esc(section.text.slice(focused.start,focused.end))+'</mark>'+esc(section.text.slice(focused.end));const mark=$('#passage-focus');mark.scrollIntoView({block:'center'});mark.focus({preventScroll:true});}
 $('#source-locator').innerHTML=`${esc(section.title)}${section.pdfPage?' · PDF page '+section.pdfPage+(section.pdfEndPage?'–'+section.pdfEndPage:''):''} · <a target="_blank" rel="noopener" href="${esc(section.pdfPage?item.pdf+'#page='+section.pdfPage:section.sourceUrl||item.sourceUrl)}">Open source location</a>`;
 }catch{if(target.isConnected)target.textContent='This text could not load. Try again with a connection, or open the original edition.'}
}
function saveAnchor(text){if(anchors.includes(text)){toast('Already in your anchors');return}if(anchors.length>=100){toast('Your shelf has 100 anchors. Remove one to make room.');return}const next=[...anchors,text];try{localStorage.setItem('antar-anchors',JSON.stringify(next));anchors=next;toast('Kept in your anchors')}catch{toast('Browser storage is unavailable. This was not saved.')}}
function clearSession(){helpIntent='understand';gentleAttempt=null;lastGentleResponse=null;stepDraft='';resetMindDraft();shelfText='';shelfTitle='';shelfLink='';shelfNeed='';shelfFile=null;activeFable=null;fableNode='start';feltNeed='';reflectionFits=false;logDraft=null;editingCheckin=null;readingNeed='understanding';readingSource='any';allowChallenging=false;catalogMood='any';catalogNeed='any';catalogSource='any';dismissedPassages.clear();openedPassages.clear();nextStep='';draft='';thoughts=[];sorts={};context='';nuance='';intensity=3;selected=[];resetStep=0;resetDone=false;go('home');toast('Current session cleared')}
document.addEventListener('click',e=>{const el=e.target.closest('button,[data-go]');if(!el)return;if(el.id==='language'){bilingual=!bilingual;render(true);return}if(el.dataset.go){go(el.dataset.go);return}if(el.dataset.quick){selected=[el.dataset.quick];nuance='';feltNeed='';reflectionFits=false;context='';go('refine');return}if(el.dataset.mood){const id=el.dataset.mood;if(selected.includes(id))selected=selected.filter(x=>x!==id);else if(selected.length<3)selected.push(id);else return toast('Choose up to three feelings');nuance='';feltNeed='';reflectionFits=false;render(true);return}if(el.dataset.nuance){nuance=nuance===el.dataset.nuance?'':el.dataset.nuance;render(true);return}if(el.dataset.sort){const i=el.dataset.sort;sorts[i]=sorts[i]===el.dataset.bucket?undefined:el.dataset.bucket;render(true);return}if(el.dataset.size){readerScale=Math.max(15,Math.min(24,readerScale+Number(el.dataset.size)));$('.reader').style.fontSize=readerScale+'px';return}if(el.dataset.remove!==undefined){const next=anchors.filter((_,i)=>i!==Number(el.dataset.remove));try{localStorage.setItem('antar-anchors',JSON.stringify(next));anchors=next;render(true)}catch{toast('Could not update browser storage')}return}const a=el.dataset.action;if(!a)return;if(a.startsWith('go-')){go(a.slice(3));return}if(a.startsWith('save-story:')){saveAnchor(stories.find(s=>s.id===a.split(':')[1]).anchor);return}switch(a){case'refine':if(!selected.length)return toast('Choose a feeling, or “Not sure”');go('refine');break;case'support':go('support');break;case'start-reset':resetStep=0;resetDone=false;go('reset');break;case'reset-next':if(resetStep<4)resetStep++;else resetDone=true;render();break;case'save-reset':saveAnchor('A quiet reset: notice 5 things I see, 4 I feel, 3 I hear, 2 I smell, and 1 I taste. I can skip or stop.');break;case'save-connection':saveAnchor('I’m having a difficult moment. Could we talk, or could you help me find support?');break;case'sort-thoughts':if(!draft.trim())return toast('Write a thought first, or choose a quiet pause');thoughts=draft.split(/\n+/).map(s=>s.trim()).filter(Boolean);sorts={};go('sort');break;case'save-step':{const input=$('#next-step');if(input.value.trim()){saveAnchor(input.value.trim());$('#step-status').textContent=anchors.includes(input.value.trim())?'Kept in your anchors.':''}else $('#step-status').textContent='Add a step, or finish without saving.';break}case'finish-thoughts':nextStep='';draft='';thoughts=[];sorts={};go('home');toast('Draft released. Only chosen anchors remain.');break;case'clear-session':clearSession();break;case'add-anchor':{const input=$('#anchor-input');if(!input.value.trim())return toast('Add a few words first');saveAnchor(input.value.trim());render(true);break}case'delete-anchors':if(anchors.length&&confirm('Delete all saved anchors from this browser?')){try{localStorage.removeItem('antar-anchors');anchors=[];render(true);toast('Saved anchors deleted')}catch{toast('Could not clear browser storage')}}break;}});
document.addEventListener('input',e=>{if(e.target.id==='next-step')nextStep=e.target.value;if(e.target.id==='thought-draft')draft=e.target.value;if(e.target.id==='custom-feeling')context=e.target.value;if(e.target.id==='intensity'){intensity=Number(e.target.value);$('#intensity-value').textContent=intensity+'/5'}if(e.target.id==='library-search'){libraryQuery=e.target.value;const q=libraryQuery.toLowerCase(),filtered=stories.filter(s=>(allowIntense||!s.sensitive)&&[s.title,s.subtitle,s.culture,s.theme].join(' ').toLowerCase().includes(q));$('#reflections').hidden=!!q&&!filtered.length;$('#book-results').innerHTML=sourcesHTML(libraryQuery);$('#story-results').innerHTML=filtered.length?filtered.map(s=>storyCard(s)).join(''):'<p class="empty">No short reflection matches. Try the book shelf below.</p>'}});
document.addEventListener('change',e=>{if(e.target.id==='intense'){allowIntense=e.target.checked;render(true)}if(e.target.id==='section-select')loadSection(Number(route.split('/')[1]),Number(e.target.value))});
window.addEventListener('hashchange',()=>render());render();
fetch('library/manifest.json').then(r=>{if(!r.ok)throw Error();return r.json()}).then(data=>{for(const item of data.sources||[]){for(const key of ['pdf','epub','original','html','text','licenseUrl']){if(item[key]&&!/^https?:/.test(item[key]))item[key]='library/'+item[key];}}sourceManifest=data;if(['library','sources','support','passages'].includes(route)||route.startsWith('source/')||route.startsWith('excerpt/'))render(true)}).catch(()=>{sourceManifest={sources:[]};if(['library','sources'].includes(route))render(true)});

loadPassages();
